                  <msPart xml:id="p1">
                     <msIdentifier>
                     </msIdentifier>
                     <msContents>
                        <summary/>
                        <msItem xml:id="p1_i1">
                           <locus from="2ra" to="3vb"/> <locus from="144ra" to="145vb"/> 
                           <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT4872MaqdemaWangel">Maqdǝma wangel</title>
                           <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                           <note>
                              The folia containing ‘Introduction to the Gospels’ are
                              misplaced. Their proper order is as follows: <locus target="#144 #2 #145 #3"/>.
                              The text appears in the following order: the first paragraph of the ‘Third period of instruction’, part of
                              the ‘Fourth period of instruction’ to the 3rd point <locus from="2ra" to="2vb"/>; 
                              the beginning of the ‘Fifth period of
                              instruction’; the ending of the ‘Fifth period of instruction’, the ‘Sixth
                              period of instruction’, the ‘Seventh period of instruction’ <locus from="3ra" to="3va"/>;
                              the ‘First period of instruction’, the ‘Second period of instruction’, the beginning of the ‘Third
                              period of instruction’ <locus target="#144rv"/>; the ‘Fourth
                              period of instruction’ from the 3rd point onwards, the ‘Third period of
                              instruction‘, the ‘Fourth period of instruction’, the first paragraph of
                              the ‘Fifth period of instruction’ <locus target="#145rv"/>.
                           </note>
                           
                           <msItem xml:id="p1_i1.1">
                              <locus from="3va" to="3vb"/>
                              <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1548Gessaw">Synopsis of classes</title>
                              <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                           </msItem>
                           
                           <msItem xml:id="p1_i1.2">
                              <locus from="3vb" to="4rb"/>
                              <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1349EpistlEusebius">Epistle of Eusebius to Carpianus (General record)</title>
                              <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                           </msItem>
                        </msItem>
               
                        <msItem xml:id="p1_i2">
                           <locus from="4rb" to="4va35"/>
                           <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1952Mashaf">Excerpt from a section called ዘኩፋሌ ‘From Kufāle’, which is devoted to the observance of the Sabbath</title>
                           <textLang mainLang="gez"/>
                           <incipit xml:lang="gez"><hi rend="rubric">በስመ፡ አብ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/>። ዝንቱ፡ ውእቱ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ዘ</hi>ይሰመይ፡ ቄደር፡ ትእዛዝ፡ በእንተ፡ ከመ፡ 
                              ንግበር፡ ፈቃዶ፡ ለእግዚአብሔር፡ ወንዘክር፡ ሕማማቲሁ፡ ዘገብረ፡ በእንቲአነ፡ </incipit>
                           <note>The excerpt comes from <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/9B88B7TK"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Yaqob1993MestirTextus"/><title level="m">Giyorgis di Saglā: Il libro del mistero &lt;hi rend="italics"&gt;(Maṣḥafa mesṭir)&lt;/hi&gt;: Parte seconda</title><title level="s">Corpus Scriptorum Christianorum Orientalium</title><author><name>Yaqob Beyene</name></author><editor><name>Yaqob Beyene</name></editor><pubPlace>Lovanii</pubPlace><publisher>In aedibus E. Peeters</publisher><date>1993</date><series><title level="s">Corpus Scriptorum Christianorum Orientalium</title><biblScope unit="volume">532, Scriptores Aethiopici, 97</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">I</biblScope><biblScope unit="volume">532, Scriptores Aethiopici, 97</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Yaqob1993MestirTextus</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Yaqob1993MestirTextus</note><citedRange unit="page">153–154</citedRange></bibl>. Despite the announcement in the incipit, the text cannot be identified with <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1959Mashaf">Maṣḥafa qedar</ref>.</note>
                        </msItem>
                        
                        <msItem xml:id="p1_i3">
                           <locus from="4va5" to="6va"/>
                           <title>Thanksgiving prayer to God from the baptismal rite</title>
                           <incipit xml:lang="gez">ንኅሥሥ፡ እንከ፡ ሕጎ፡ ወንባርኮ፡ ለእግዚአብሔር፡ ወናእኵቶ፡ በእንተ፡ ኵሉ፡ ዘጸገወነ፡ ሠናይቶ፡ ለውሉደ፡ ሰብእ፡፡ ወእምዝ፡ ተአቢ፡ እምኵሉ፡ ዕለት፡ ትንሣኤሁ፡ ቅድስት፡ ዘመሐረነ፡ እግዚእነ፡ ወመድኃኒነ፡ ወፈጣሪነ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ቃለ፡ ዘተወልደ፡ 
                              እምቅድመ፡ ይትፈጠር፡ ዓለም፡</incipit> 
                           <note>The prayer is most likely an excerpt from a larger liturgical text concerning baptism. 
                              It is followed by three readings from the New Testament <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3519Epistle">Eph. 6: 10–24</ref>, <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1019Actsof">Act. 12: 6–11</ref>, 
                              <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1882MarkGo">Mk. 16: 32–37</ref> and two prayers over water:
                              <q xml:lang="gez">በእንተ፡ ጸሎት፡ ዘይትነበበ፡ ዲበ፡ ማይ፡</q> and <q xml:lang="gez">ወካዕበ፡ ይጸልዩ፡ ለሐዲሳን፡ እለተጠምቁ፡</q>
                              This text cannot be identified with <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1959Mashaf">Maṣḥafa qedar</ref> either.</note>
                        </msItem>
               
                        <msItem xml:id="p1_i4">
                           <locus target="#143"/> <locus from="147va" to="148ra"/>
                           <title>Teaching on Christian life</title>
                           <incipit xml:lang="am">ቍጣም፡ ሲመጻ፡ ልብንና፡ መላስን፡ ይጠብቀዋል፡ ልቡንና፡ መላስን፡ ያልጠበቀ፡ ሰው፡ ከክፉ፡ ነገር፡ ይወድቃል፡ መዓትም፡ ወዓማፂ፡ አይክል፡ ጸዲቀ፡ እንዳለ፡ ሲራክ፡ ቍጣ፡ ሲመጻ፡ ይታገሠዋል፡ ኋላ፡ ደስ፡ ያሰኛልና፡ 
                              ተገሣ፡ በመዓት፡ ወድኅረ፡ ታስተፌስሐከ፡ እንዳለ፡ ሲራክ፡</incipit>
                           <textLang mainLang="am" otherLangs="gez"/>
                        </msItem>
                        
                        <msItem xml:id="p1_i5">
                           <locus from="146ra" to="147rb"/>
                           <title type="incomplte" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2317Senodo">Likely an excerpt from ‘Senodos’</title>
                           <incipit xml:lang="gez">ወካዕበ፡ ዘሀበከ፡ ትእምርተ፡ ለትንሣኤሁ፡ ለክርስቶስ፡ ዘእንተ፡ ሰቀልኮ፡ ዘሠናየ፡ ገብረ፡ ለከ። ወእምጣብርናተ፡ ፈርዖን፡ ንጉሠ፡ ግብጽ፡ ዘአውጽአከ፡ እንተ፡ ባሕረ፡ ኤርትራ፡ ከመ፡ ዘየሐውር፡ በየብስ፡ </incipit>
                        </msItem>
                     </msContents>
                     
